  "result": "Perfect! All 92 tests pass. I've successfully implemented line discounts for the invoicing system:\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`:**\n- Added DISCOUNT_INVALID error code\n\n**Updated `src/invoices.js`:**\n- Added `isValidDiscountPercent()` validation function\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, total }` where:\n  - `discount` = sum of (line total \u00d7 discountPercent \u00f7 100) for each line, rounded with `roundCents()`\n  - `total` = subtotal \u2212 discount, clamped at 0 using `Math.max(0, subtotal - discount)`\n- Updated `createInvoice()` to accept optional `discountPercent` in line input\n  - Validates discountPercent is a number between 0-100 (can be decimal like 12.5)\n  - Returns DISCOUNT_INVALID for invalid values\n  - Stores discountPercent on each line (defaults to 0 if omitted)\n- Updated `addLine()` with same discount validation and handling\n\n**Updated tests:**\n- Fixed existing invoiceTotals tests to include discount field\n- Added 11 new discount tests covering:\n  - Discount acceptance and defaults\n  - Validation of discount bounds and type\n  - Decimal discounts (12.5%)\n  - Fractional discount rounding\n  - Total clamping at 0 (100% discount)\n  - Mixed discount percentages\n  - Render tests with discounts applied\n\nAll 92 tests pass (76 previous + 16 new). The project now properly handles line discounts with fractional rounding and ensures no amounts go below zero.",
